**Root-level exceptions.** Only these may sit outside `docs/`, and neither may be moved:

| File | Why it cannot move |
|---|---|
| `CLAUDE.md` | Claude Code scans the project root at startup. Moved, it is never found, and every session runs without project context |
| `README.md` | Rendered as the repository homepage |

`CLAUDE.md` must stay a thin pointer to the entry point plus any mandatory behavioural rules. It
must not grow into a second entry point — two files claiming to be the starting point guarantees
they disagree.

## 2. The single entry point rule

<!-- DECIDE: name the file that is this project's entry point, and use that name throughout this
     section. It is whatever `.design-suite/docs.manifest.json` maps the entry-point role to — for
     an application usually an instructions document, for a package usually the docs `README`. One
     file, named here, and never a second one. -->

**The entry point named above is the single entry point for all documentation.**

1. Every task starts by reading it.
2. Every document in `docs/` must be registered in its companion table. An unregistered document
   does not exist from the entry point's perspective.
3. When you add, move, or remove a document, update that table **in the same change**.

The entry point must never fork.

